{"hits": {"hits": [{"created": "2022-06-27T15:41:54.263513+00:00", "modified": "2022-07-18T07:40:31.723487+00:00", "id": 6761040, "conceptrecid": "6761039", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.6761040", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.6761039", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6761040", "metadata": {"title": "Supporting Information for \"Wave heating during the helium flash and lithium-enhanced clump stars\"", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.6761040", "publication_date": "2022-06-27", "description": "<p>&quot;data&quot; contains the data used to generate the plots in this paper.</p>\n\n<p>&quot;batches&quot; contains a log of nearly every MESA run performed in this work (including ~all failed experiments). These are stored as Python3 Pickle files. Experiments were run using the RemoteExperiments software package (https://github.com/adamjermyn/remote_experiments). See the documentation there for&nbsp;further information on the data format for these files.</p>\n\n<p>&quot;Stokes_Experiments&quot; contains a git repository which includes both the final version of the code used in our canonical run as well as the full history of (nearly) all experiments we performed along the way. Each experiment is a commit (detached from any branch) with the commit message &quot;patch&quot;.</p>\n\n<p>&quot;Scripts&quot; contains both the scripts we used to run these experiments and those we used to analyze them and make the plots in the paper.</p>\n\n<p>Further detail is given in the paper itself.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Adam S. Jermyn", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Jim Fuller", "affiliation": null}], "version": "v1", "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "communities": [{"id": "mesa"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "6761039"}}]}}, "title": "Supporting Information for \"Wave heating during the helium flash and lithium-enhanced clump stars\"", "